    docs(mark): implementation plan for the cube mark (PV3-35)

    Six tasks, each with its own test cycle: the piece table, rotation and
    back-face culling, projection to polygons, the component and the ✳ removal,
    the canvas upgrade, and the ship gate.

    Every number in the plan was run before it was written: 35 pieces at full
    detail and 17 below the 24px threshold, three visible faces on an isometric
    cube and one head-on, and no polygon outside its box at any size or angle.

    Also names the three existing tests the ✳ removal breaks — footer.test.ts
    expects the glyph, tokens.test.ts requires the `think` keyframes, and
    a11y.test.ts sweeps the glyph for aria-hidden — so none of them is a surprise
    mid-task.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
